2026-09-17T04:04:40.6406040Z Some notable sight was drawing the passengers, both men and women, to
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6406294Z the window; and therefore I rose and crossed the car to see what it was.
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6406546Z I saw near the track an enclosure, and round it some laughing men, and
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6406791Z inside it some whirling dust, and amid the dust some horses, plunging,
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6407179Z huddling, and dodging. They were cow ponies in a corral, and one of them
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6407467Z would not be caught, no matter who threw the rope. We had plenty of time
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6407720Z to watch this sport, for our train had stopped that the engine might
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6408049Z take water at the tank before it pulled us up beside the station
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6408292Z platform of Medicine Bow. We were also six hours late, and starving for
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6408548Z entertainment. The pony in the corral was wise, and rapid of limb. Have
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6408793Z you seen a skilful boxer watch his antagonist with a quiet, incessant
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6409168Z eye? Such an eye as this did the pony keep upon whatever man took the
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6409419Z rope. The man might pretend to look at the weather, which was fine; or
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6409667Z he might affect earnest conversation with a bystander: it was bootless.
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6409911Z The pony saw through it. No feint hoodwinked him. This animal was
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6410147Z thoroughly a man of the world. His undistracted eye stayed fixed upon
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6410392Z the dissembling foe, and the gravity of his horse-expression made the
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6410758Z matter one of high comedy. Then the rope would sail out at him, but he
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6411056Z was already elsewhere; and if horses laugh, gayety must have abounded in
2026-09-17T04:04:40.6411311Z that corral. Sometimes the pony took a turn alone; next he had slid in a
